//  The string operations are builtin *functions*, not methods: `startsWith(s, x)`, not
//  `s.startsWith(x)`. Fourteen of them exist, which makes this the shape people write, so
//  the diagnostic names the rewrite instead of only saying the method does not exist.
function main():void {
    string s = "hello.txt";
    print(s.startsWith("he"));
    eof: pass;
}
